This app is pretty much one half of the system I made for a small grocery shop.
They wanted a nice looking website, capable of showing their items in a dynamic way, schedualing discounts, etc..
The idea was to create a Web App to be used in whatever divice, as well as an API written in Laravel which would act as the unique source of truth for the whole system.
It included a way for people to do their shopping online whithout the need to log in, involving a simple purchase which would be stored in the system.
A code would be generated and, for the client, stored in browser and sent via email. 
In the admin dashboard the owners could see the purchase and get it ready, the client would only have to go to the store and just pick it up.
Or the owners could deliver. The system is intetionally made to let them choose what they want, including if they want to disable purchasing.
Its an app for a small store, so this bigger luxuries can be taken without any troubble to great benefit. These luxuries also included no log in required for the clients.
All purchases would be tracked via the browser history and trough the emails sent.
The system used external APIs, namely Amazon's SES (for sending emails) and AWS (for storing images and backups)
